    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d202">

                <pb facs="0355" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg267"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Sir Julian Pauncefote.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 5th instant,
                    in reference to the case of John Gibbons and family, declared to be assisted
                    immigrants likely to become public charges, I have the honor to inform you that
                    prior to the receipt of your note the Commissioner of Immigration at New York
                    had been instructed by telegraph, at the instance of the British Consul-General
                    at New York, to detain the immigrants for a further investigation of the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
